hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20945","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Asim ibn Hilal informed us, Ghadarah ibn Urwah al-Fuqaymi narrated to us, Abu Urwah narrated to me, he said: We were waiting for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he came out with his head dripping from ablution or bath, and he prayed. When he finished the prayer, the people began asking him: O Messenger of Allah, is there blame upon us in such. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No, O people, the religion of Allah, mighty and majestic, is in ease, saying it three times. And Yazid once said: The people began saying: O Messenger of Allah, what do we say in such, what do we say in such."
